{{ill|Reki Hakase|lt=Doctor of Calendar|ja|暦博士|1=Reki Hakase|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Reki Hakase|13=User:Immanuelle/Reki Hakase|qq=}} is a topic related to   [[Onmyodo]]

__NOINDEX__
'''Reki Hakase''' ({{ill|暦博士|ja|暦博士|1=Reki Hakase|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/暦博士|13=User:Immanuelle/Reki Hakase|qq=}}) was a position within Japan's [[Ritsuryō system]], under the [[Ministry of Central Affairs|Nakatsukasashō]] and its {{ill|Onmyōryō|ja|陰陽寮|1=Yin-Yang Bureau|2=ja|3=陰陽寮|4=fr|5=Bureau d'Onmyō|6=zh|7=阴阳寮|8=ko|9=음양료|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Onmyōryō|13=User:Immanuelle/Yin-Yang Bureau|qq=}} bureau. The role involved the annual creation of calendars ({{ill|暦|ja|暦|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/暦|qq=}}), revisions ({{ill|改暦|ja|改暦|1=Calendar reform|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/改暦|13=User:Immanuelle/Calendar reform|qq=}}), solar eclipse predictions, and education of calendrical students ({{ill|暦生|ja|暦生|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/暦生|qq=}}). The position was originally limited to one official (later expanded with an additional adjunct), with a Rank equivalent to {{ill|Junior Seventh Rank, Upper Grade|ja|従七位上|1=Junior Seventh Rank|lt=Junior Seventh Rank, Upper Grade|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Junior Seventh Rank, Upper Grade|13=User:Immanuelle/Junior Seventh Rank|qq=}}. Over time, holders of the position typically held Ranks of {{ill|Fifth Rank|ja|五位|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Fifth Rank|qq=}} or higher. The position's traditional Japanese reading is "Koyomi no Hakase," and the Tang Chinese name was "Saireki" or "Saireki Seihō."

== Overview ==
The earliest mention of the position appears in the {{ill|Nihon Shoki|ja|日本書紀|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Nihon Shoki|qq=}}, which records a request in the 14th year of Emperor {{ill|Kinmei|ja|欽明天皇|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kinmei|qq=}}'s reign (553) for the kingdom of {{ill|Baekje|ja|百済|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Baekje|qq=}} to send calendrical specialists to Japan. This request, made during heightened military tensions with {{ill|Silla|ja|新羅|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Silla|qq=}}, likely reflected a quid pro quo for Japan's military aid to Baekje. Scholars suggest that Baekje preferred only to provide annual calendars rather than train Japanese officials in calendrical science ({{ill|暦学|ja|暦学|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/暦学|qq=}}). This reliance delayed the institutional establishment of the position until later periods, following the transmission of calendrical knowledge by figures like {{ill|Kanroku|ja|観勒|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kanroku|qq=}}.

In {{ill|Enryaku|ja|延暦|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Enryaku|qq=}} 10 (791), the office received an allotment of three ''shō'' (units) of rice fields for its operation. Early holders of the post were often {{ill|渡来人|ja|渡来人|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/渡来人|qq=}} families versed in {{ill|暦道|ja|暦道|1=Rekidō|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/暦道|13=User:Immanuelle/Rekidō|qq=}} (calendrical studies) and {{ill|算道|1=Sandō_(mathematics)|2=ja|3=算道|lt=Sandō|ja|算道|1=Sandō_(mathematics)|2=ja|3=算道|lt=Sandō|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/算道|13=User:Immanuelle/Sandō_(mathematics)|qq=}} (mathematical studies). Over time, native Japanese families such as the {{ill|Ōharu no Ason|ja|大春日氏|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ōharu no Ason|qq=}}, {{ill|Ie-no-Miyako clan|ja|家原氏|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ie-no-Miyako clan|qq=}}, {{ill|Ōnakatomi clan|ja|大中臣氏|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ōnakatomi clan|qq=}}, and {{ill|Kamo no Asomi clan|ja|賀茂朝臣氏|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kamo no Asomi clan|qq=}} became hereditary holders.

Prominent figures associated with the position include {{ill|Ōharu Manomaro|ja|大春日真野麻呂|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ōharu Manomaro|qq=}}, who advocated for adopting the {{ill|Goki Calendar|ja|五紀暦|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Goki Calendar|qq=}} and {{ill|Senmyō Calendar|ja|宣明暦|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Senmyō Calendar|qq=}} during Emperor {{ill|Seiwa|ja|Emperor Seiwa|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Seiwa|qq=}}'s reign, and {{ill|Kibi no Makibi|ja|吉備真備|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kibi no Makibi|qq=}}, credited with introducing the {{ill|Dai'en Calendar|ja|大衍暦|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Dai'en Calendar|qq=}} to Japan. The 10th-century scholar {{ill|Kamo no Tadayuki|ja|賀茂忠行|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kamo no Tadayuki|qq=}} and his son, {{ill|Kamo no Yasunori|ja|賀茂保憲|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kamo no Yasunori|qq=}}, were notable successors. After Yasunori's death, his descendants retained the ''rekidō'' lineage, while his student {{ill|Abe no Seimei|ja|安倍晴明|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Abe no Seimei|qq=}}'s family carried on the {{ill|天文道|ja|天文道|1=Tenmondō (astrology)|lt=Tenmondō|qq= (astrology)|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/天文道|13=User:Immanuelle/Tenmondō (astrology)|qq=}} tradition.

Private possession of calendrical texts was strictly regulated under the {{ill|雑令|ja|雑令|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/雑令|qq=}}, particularly the ''Hisho Genjōryō,'' which inhibited the cultivation of external talent. This restriction proved significant during periods of political upheaval, such as {{ill|Taira no Masakado|ja|Taira no Masakado|1=Taira no Masakado|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Taira no Masakado|13=User:Immanuelle/Taira no Masakado|qq=}}'s attempt to establish a rival court and the {{ill|Southern Court (Japan)|ja|南朝|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Southern Court (Japan)|qq=}} during the {{ill|Nanboku-chō period|ja|南北朝時代|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Nanboku-chō period|qq=}}, neither of which could appoint a ''Reki Hakase'' or produce official calendars for their respective eras.

When the main line of the Kamo family went extinct, the {{ill|Kōtokui Family|lt=Kōtokui Family|lt=Kōtokui clan|ja|幸徳井家|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kōtokui clan|qq=}}, a cadet branch, assumed the position. {{ill|Kōtokui Tomokage|ja|幸徳井友景|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kōtokui Tomokage|qq=}}, a prominent figure, passed the office to his grandson {{ill|Kōtokui Tomotsuna|ja|幸徳井友傳|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kōtokui Tomotsuna|qq=}}. Over time, the family's influence waned as the {{ill|Tsuchimikado family|ja|土御門家|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Tsuchimikado family|qq=}} in {{ill|Onmyōdō|ja|陰陽道|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Onmyōdō|qq=}} and the {{ill|Bakufu Tenmonkata|ja|天文方|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Bakufu Tenmonkata|qq=}} in calendrical studies gradually overshadowed their role. Eventually, the Kōtokui family focused on {{ill|暦注|ja|暦注|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/暦注|qq=}} annotation alone. Following the abolition of the Onmyōryō during the {{ill|Meiji Restoration|ja|明治維新|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Meiji Restoration|qq=}}, the position of ''Reki Hakase'' was discontinued, and its functions ceased with the adoption of the {{ill|Gregorian calendar|1=Gregorian calendar|2=ja|3=グレゴリオ暦|4=fr|5=Calendrier grégorien|6=de|7=Gregorianischer Kalender|8=tl|9=Kalendaryong Gregoryano|10=ru|11=Григорианский календарь|ja|太陽暦|1=Solar calendar|2=ja|3=太陽暦|4=de|5=Solarkalender|6=fr|7=Calendrier solaire|8=it|9=Calendario solare|10=ru|11=Солнечный календарь|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Gregorian calendar|13=User:Immanuelle/Gregorian calendar|qq=}}.

